sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 85.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Same onset law as Pass 1: Schnakenberg (a, b) = (0.10, 0.90), Dv/Du = 9, λ_c = 184.3 µm = 0.0001843 m, Holocene age 0 Ma, eight-wavelength periodic patch. The nonlinear run now starts from noise (seed 3107) plus a shallow domain-scale source gradient, and the dominant shell that emerges is n = 8 (184.3 µm). Band-weighted wavelength is 176.47 µm. Continuum versus periodic-shell sweep: Pearson r = 0.9996, RMSE = 2.02 µm. Ratio sweep 9 → 14 moves the fastest wavelength from 187.2 µm to 212.1 µm. Ablation Dv = Du keeps max σ = −0.10. Specimen dark fraction 0.380 versus model 0.314; coherency 0.485 versus 0.904; luminance KS = 0.302; radial-spectrum r = 0.910. Computer-vision similarity of the 12-frame 640 px GIF against the micrograph is 87.5. The micrograph still has no scale bar. Overall 85.2/100 (faithfulness 83.8, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit dddc48a7fadc3d15f0038b8b8ef2a781309b9d10; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 87, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at dddc48a7fadc3d15f0038b8b8ef2a781309b9d10, image/gif, 1612487 B, 640×640 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 8d6fd506a2a8af42acd5599713ba2dff5c7880d382002709b0279f26beed9fd4 (sha256 8d6fd506a2a8af42acd5599713ba2dff5c7880d382002709b0279f26beed9fd4), spec_fingerprint 948f3bc47cbf1c637386574fa0406a35e731104672ab92814b20a045ca1592e1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 948f3bc47cbf1c637386574fa0406a35e731104672ab92814b20a045ca1592e1; artifact_sha256: 8d6fd506a2a8af42acd5599713ba2dff5c7880d382002709b0279f26beed9fd4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0/ambystoma_mexicanum_chromatophores_specimen.jpg=cc106cdbb5c28a40..., datasets/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0/ambystoma_mexicanum_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=5047ff540b2f84a0...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and diffusion-driven instability | Murray 1981 coat pre-pattern and domain-growth scale argument | Epperlein & Löfberg 1989 larval Ambystoma mexicanum pigment pattern | Frost-Mason & Mason 1996 review of axolotl pigmentation; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters with Du set so the onset wavelength is 184.3 µm | Noise-seeded spectral integration and a shallow source gradient of amplitude 0.12 | Periodic-shell quantization of the continuum wavelength, ratio sweep, and Dv = Du ablation | Quantile segmentation and structure-tensor coherency of the CC BY-SA micrograph; transfer_boundary: 184.3 µm is the slot scale coordinate, not a number measured on the photograph | The source gradient is a reconstruction that keeps the patch from crystallizing; it is not in the constant-coefficient Turing paper | Adult ocellus size is a longer scale of this same Holocene species, not a successor chronospecies; does_not_claim: That stellate melanophore geometry is generated by the PDE | A micrometre scale bar on the Wikimedia micrograph | A second independent assessor." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Partly resolved from Pass 1 R4: the field is a broken labyrinth rather than a crystal. Coherency is still 0.904 versus 0.485, so stellate cell geometry is not claimed.",
            "remediation needed: R5 remains open: this pass is still a single assessor (Grok 4.7). No second provider was available, and none was invented.",
            "remediation needed: Resolved from Pass 1 R1: the cos+cos lattice is no longer the initial condition. The n=8 shell is selected from noise.",
            "remediation needed: Resolved from Pass 1 R2: periodic-shell comparison gives Pearson r 0.999595 and RMSE 2.02 µm, not a bitwise copy of the reference 1.",
            "remediation needed: Resolved from Pass 1 R3: the dispersion cusp is labeled as the disc=0 branch point and sampled on 900 wavenumbers." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.852"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; second provider still not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

